prompt:
## Resumo
DentaVoice is a medical-grade interface characterized by high information density, monochromatic clarity, and semantic functional highlighting. It balances complex data entry (dental charting) with live-feedback voice controls.

## Estilo Visual
# One-shot prompt: build the DentaVoice dental charting prototype EXACTLY

Build **DentaVoice**, an AI voice-dictation dental charting prototype: a single-page web app (plain HTML + CSS + vanilla JavaScript, no frameworks, no build step). A dentist dictates during an exam ("26 MOD caries, plan composite") and the AI performs structured charting — odontogram + chart-entries table on the left, dictation panel (mic, settings, transcript & AI-logged actions) on the right.

**Create exactly three code files. Write out the provided source VERBATIM — character for character, no reformatting, no renaming, no "improvements", no added comments. The code is the specification.**

1. `index.html` — the exact contents of Source File 1
2. `styles.css` — the exact contents of Source File 2
3. `app.js` — the exact contents of Source File 3

The logo is generic and drawn entirely in code (a 26px black rounded square with a white waveform glyph plus the "DentaVoice" wordmark as text) — no logo image is needed. The only image asset is `avatar.png` (the patient photo, a square image shown as a 32px circle): use the attached file if provided, otherwise substitute any placeholder square image with that filename so the page still renders.

When done, verify: open `index.html` — the page must open **mid-exam, complete and active**: the mic is live (black button with animated equalizer bars and a spinning multi-color gradient ring, blue pulsing "Listening" pill, caption "Listening — speak naturally"), the odontogram shows the full charted exam (blue fills on teeth 16/17/18/46, red MOD caries on 26, blue crown ring on 36, amber watch fill on 44, tooth 25 faded with a grey ✕ for missing, red extraction ✕ on 38), the table reads "11 entries" with count pills 6 existing / 3 planned / 1 missing, and the transcript shows every utterance with its action cards. Press **Play demo exam** — the chart resets to the 3-entry seeded start ("18 buccal composite, 17 palatal composite, 17 buccal amalgam") and the exam dictates itself back in, line by line; `index.html?demo` triggers the same on load. If a DESIGN.md accompanies this prompt, it explains design intent (tokens, typography, components) — but where prose and code disagree, THE CODE WINS.

